1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Both the science and social studies tests are built around source material. You are given a passage, a graph, a map, or a document, and asked to interpret it. Background knowledge helps you read faster, but the answer is nearly always in front of you. This is good news for adult learners, who are often far better at reasoning from evidence than at recalling school facts."}]
